		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3D7C8C36A2896D4E"]
			description: [
				"The Superheavy chart gave you the &6OpV Machine Casing&r. The hull waits for parts nobody has made yet."
				"The bulge is crowded and very old. Terzan 5 is a fossil of the early galaxy, and Sagittarius A* sits at its centre."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:opv_machine_casing"
			id: "7C074BF11FC1790D"
			rewards: [{ id: "326CDD931F7FD469", type: "xp", xp: 50 }]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{ id: "3BDE3E7A2D979F0D", item: "gtceu:opv_machine_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "The Galactic Bulge"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1A9EE7510BD6DBFC"]
			description: ["Three places lie ahead: a magnetar for chain matter, Cygnus X-1 for antimatter and the Kugelblitz, and a globular cluster for probes. The machine and circuit tabs hold the parts, and the integration tab holds the power."]
			icon: "gtceu:opv_machine_casing"
			id: "1184DDEA5D8984CC"
			rewards: [{ id: "3DFCF46951DE4A55", type: "xp", xp: 25 }]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "54400E133A600EA5", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "The Way In"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1184DDEA5D8984CC"]
			description: ["A relay seed is the first thing you send to the bulge. A pasta-strand magsail brakes it on the thin gas between the stars. The seed is made from UXV parts only."]
			icon: "grindless:bulge_relay_seed"
			id: "73394B2C6D508B8A"
			rewards: [{ id: "3D05C7C6B14F3C3D", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "53A5A08F82D1A1BB", item: "grindless:bulge_relay_seed", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bulge Relay"
			x: 7.5d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["73394B2C6D508B8A"]
			description: [
				"The warp gate throws the seed across the dark between the arm and the bulge. Nothing comes back, and that is the idea."
				"The gate is fiction. The magsail braking it uses is real physics."
			]
			icon: "grindless:launched_bulge_seed"
			id: "1334D64ED6E948AA"
			rewards: [{ id: "5350FDD7C3857C6B", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "5685081BFB1C071D", item: "grindless:launched_bulge_seed", type: "item" }]
			title: "Seed Away"
			x: 10.0d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1334D64ED6E948AA"]
			description: ["The seed unfolds a platform in orbit around a magnetar. Its field is about a thousand trillion times Earth's, strong enough to bend atoms into chains. Chain matter, field-frozen plate and positron cells come from here and nowhere else."]
			icon: "grindless:launched_bulge_seed"
			id: "7F4169BDA6339C6F"
			rewards: [{ id: "3D7DDAF9F2688F6B", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			tasks: [{ dimension: "grindless:sgr1806_orbit", id: "550CFB430F467A0F", type: "dimension" }]
			title: "SGR 1806-20"
			x: 12.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1334D64ED6E948AA"]
			description: ["The first image from the bulge. It shows where the debris, the nodes and the old stars are, and the gate keeps it."]
			icon: "grindless:bulge_chart"
			id: "32FA798856B28769"
			rewards: [{ id: "13758CD8892FDE4C", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1D29CC0DFA9616E1", item: "grindless:bulge_chart", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bulge Chart"
			x: 12.5d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F4169BDA6339C6F"]
			description: ["The pasta machines skim the magnetar's crust, cage each phase and draw it into an &6ingot&r of chain-like matter. Chain strand is fiction. The crust and its field are real."]
			icon: "gtceu:chain_strand_ingot"
			id: "7C75640ED457CEA4"
			rewards: [{ id: "759BDD63EE457C15", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3EAB9DDF35F8F1DE", item: "gtceu:chain_strand_ingot", type: "item" }]
			title: "Chain Strand"
			x: 15.0d
			y: -8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C75640ED457CEA4"]
			description: ["The strand is drawn into wire, braided in PBO and sheathed. The &6Chain Strand Cable&r carries OpV power."]
			icon: "gtceu:chain_strand_single_cable"
			id: "592D27E5456D4D25"
			rewards: [{ id: "15E0DCD05FF66CEA", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "358919E74C27DFB3", item: "gtceu:chain_strand_single_cable", type: "item" }]
			title: "Chain Strand Cable"
			x: 17.5d
			y: -10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C75640ED457CEA4"]
			description: ["Sheets of strand lattice are laminated with lasagna plate into a &6Chain Lamina Stack&r for the hull plates."]
			icon: "grindless:chain_lamina_stack"
			id: "3BF1C2F89049EA90"
			rewards: [{ id: "5B38FBEF46417AE1", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7B9BCD4B6E699BFB", item: "grindless:chain_lamina_stack", type: "item" }]
			title: "Chain Lamina"
			x: 17.5d
			y: -8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["592D27E5456D4D25", "3BF1C2F89049EA90"]
			description: ["The &6OpV Machine Hull&r joins the casing, the cable and the lamina stack. Every OpV machine starts from one."]
			icon: "gtceu:opv_machine_hull"
			id: "59A06A2C9ADDA9E4"
			rewards: [{ id: "71FCD98513284F86", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7626DF10C6668F4D", item: "gtceu:opv_machine_hull", type: "item" }]
			title: "OpV Hull"
			x: 20.0d
			y: -8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["592D27E5456D4D25"]
			description: ["A magnetar's field is strong enough to turn gamma rays into pairs of electrons and positrons. A magnetic converter here seals the positrons into a &6Dense Positron Cell&r, and the antihydrogen line needs it."]
			icon: "grindless:dense_positron_cell"
			id: "7BDABCDAEB2DA9E2"
			rewards: [{ id: "107EF7553DCC25DF", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "765BB9862A2ABFCD", item: "grindless:dense_positron_cell", type: "item" }]
			title: "Dense Positron Cell"
			x: 20.0d
			y: -10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32FA798856B28769"]
			description: ["Dies are bumped, bonded and tested near absolute zero, then put together as a &6Tetron Array&r. The gate keeps one."]
			icon: "grindless:tetron_array"
			id: "391E9FA027FD4A64"
			rewards: [{ id: "3A00381FA1827FF0", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "12A4BD4E54A4A564", item: "grindless:tetron_array", type: "item" }]
			title: "Tetron Array"
			x: 17.5d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32FA798856B28769"]
			description: ["The black hole's companion is still there, and now the platform serves a different job. The beams, the antimatter and the Kugelblitz are made here."]
			icon: "gtceu:annihilation_engine"
			id: "7B1E66BC13548877"
			rewards: [{ id: "3B807DAD020D12AD", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ dimension: "grindless:cygnus_x1_orbit", id: "51FFA7ACBC795F17", type: "dimension" }]
			title: "Back to Cygnus X-1"
			x: 15.0d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B1E66BC13548877"]
			description: ["A thin beryllium foil lets the proton beam out and keeps the vacuum in. Brazed and tested, it is the &6Beam Window&r."]
			icon: "grindless:be_beam_window"
			id: "58C89E98AE7966A6"
			rewards: [{ id: "57A77E70AAE9CAF9", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1B87B0D1BADDCEC1", item: "grindless:be_beam_window", type: "item" }]
			title: "Beam Window"
			x: 17.5d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["58C89E98AE7966A6"]
			description: ["Protons strike an iridium target, and a decelerator slows what comes out until a trap can hold it. The trap stacks the antiprotons into an &6Antiproton Stack&r. Half of them are lost to annihilation, so handle the stack with care."]
			icon: "grindless:antiproton_stack_opv"
			id: "125A9489212645EA"
			rewards: [{ id: "36E5B787221E8C43", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7FA6F79EE2BF71DB", item: "grindless:antiproton_stack_opv", type: "item" }]
			title: "Antiproton Stack"
			x: 20.0d
			y: -5.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["125A9489212645EA", "7BDABCDAEB2DA9E2"]
			description: ["An antiproton and a positron make antihydrogen, and a magnetic trap keeps it off the walls. Cooled by a Lyman-alpha laser, it freezes into an &6Antihydrogen Ice Cell&r."]
			icon: "grindless:antihydrogen_ice_cell"
			id: "38F0C34A187A7746"
			rewards: [{ id: "771FFEDD10D4EA6C", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7F7A1FE2DC035588", item: "grindless:antihydrogen_ice_cell", type: "item" }]
			title: "Antihydrogen Ice"
			x: 22.5d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B1E66BC13548877", "391E9FA027FD4A64"]
			description: ["A lead beam fired into a target gives a fireball, and the distiller picks the seed of a strangelet out of it. A strangelet is a hypothesis. The seed is fiction."]
			icon: "grindless:strangelet_seed"
			id: "3E5E07D88B48C85B"
			rewards: [{ id: "5D5EEA5D4C3CEA1C", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3A798540A529756A", item: "grindless:strangelet_seed", type: "item" }]
			title: "Strangelet Seed"
			x: 20.0d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3E5E07D88B48C85B"]
			description: ["The vault grows the seed by feeding it neutrons until it is stable. A stable strangelet is not observed. In this pack it is a fuel, and the gate keeps one."]
			icon: "grindless:stable_exotic_matter"
			id: "51C0DDF70D599BE7"
			rewards: [{ id: "3D7B85F62B079B78", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "72F81A4E7795C67F", item: "grindless:stable_exotic_matter", type: "item" }]
			title: "Stable Exotic Matter"
			x: 22.5d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["51C0DDF70D599BE7", "38F0C34A187A7746"]
			description: ["Light so dense it collapses into a black hole. The forge holds the seed, and the result is the &6Kugelblitz Core&r. A real Kugelblitz is only a prediction of general relativity. Here it is made on purpose, and the gate consumes it."]
			icon: "grindless:kugelblitz_core"
			id: "7808A81BF8AA169E"
			rewards: [{ id: "7B1C168616DB9197", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7CF1CC6E41D19701", item: "grindless:kugelblitz_core", type: "item" }]
			title: "Kugelblitz Core"
			x: 25.0d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7808A81BF8AA169E"]
			description: ["A black hole radiates, and the drive points that radiation one way. Globular clusters hold too little gas for a magsail, so the probe to Terzan 5 brakes on this drive."]
			icon: "grindless:hawking_drive"
			id: "1C5A8ECE70B119DD"
			rewards: [{ id: "5CDAB77BE39D324F", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "33E7A7C45D2D3C8C", item: "grindless:hawking_drive", type: "item" }]
			title: "Hawking Drive"
			x: 27.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1C5A8ECE70B119DD"]
			description: ["Nickel-64 from the magnetar and californium make elements 124 and 126, and the superheavy lab records them. Element 126 is fiction here: the real island of stability has not been found."]
			icon: "grindless:superheavy_census_iv"
			id: "5D3CA36016CD74E2"
			rewards: [{ id: "11DDEBB00A2F8095", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "34324876E068134F", item: "grindless:superheavy_census_iv", type: "item" }]
			title: "Superheavy Census IV"
			x: 30.0d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5D3CA36016CD74E2"]
			description: ["A probe with a tetron array, an XNAV unit and a Hawking drive brakes into the cluster by itself. The gate throws it, and it opens a ring at the other end."]
			icon: "grindless:launched_pathfinder"
			id: "590B0DB9B61FA40E"
			rewards: [{ id: "1783FBEEB72BC244", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "146ED91622026A79", item: "grindless:launched_pathfinder", type: "item" }]
			title: "The Pathfinder"
			x: 32.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["590B0DB9B61FA40E"]
			description: ["Terzan 5 is a globular cluster, a ball of very old stars packed tight at the galaxy's centre. Its core is the last place before Sagittarius A*. Debris, metal and starlight are all here."]
			icon: "grindless:probe_seed"
			id: "34EC6937B4EB1880"
			rewards: [{ id: "3E337F23B28CDFBA", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			tasks: [{ dimension: "grindless:terzan5_core", id: "770E823F16425015", type: "dimension" }]
			title: "Terzan 5"
			x: 35.0d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["34EC6937B4EB1880"]
			description: ["The core is strewn with debris that no atmosphere has weathered. The debris harvester collects it as feed for the probes."]
			icon: "grindless:bulge_debris"
			id: "53687208B5A566FC"
			rewards: [{ id: "1BF5C349DB5CFDD5", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1A7A564582E14B9B", item: "grindless:bulge_debris", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bulge Debris"
			x: 37.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["53687208B5A566FC"]
			description: ["A probe that copies itself. Terzan 5 supplies the metal, and a kit from home supplies what the cluster cannot. Self-replication is fiction here; a real one is far away."]
			icon: "grindless:probe_seed"
			id: "5FCBAB1702AAE56B"
			rewards: [{ id: "53EABB21EA6BAFF3", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "5567C58E9D77131A", item: "grindless:probe_seed", type: "item" }]
			title: "Probe Seed"
			x: 40.0d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5FCBAB1702AAE56B"]
			description: ["Every copy needs a shell. The refinery sinters cluster silicate into a &6Cluster Sinter Casing&r, and no copy leaves without one."]
			icon: "grindless:cluster_sinter_casing"
			id: "5DB4AECF2C68DD7A"
			rewards: [{ id: "580D6301AE02AE28", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7B7E5BAA6A0A570F", item: "grindless:cluster_sinter_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Sinter Casing"
			x: 42.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5DB4AECF2C68DD7A"]
			description: ["Each seed carries collector nodes out into the swarm, where they unfold and begin to collect starlight. A pack is consumed as it degrades, so the supply must never stop."]
			icon: "grindless:deployed_node_pack"
			id: "1272CCD5EF9968D8"
			rewards: [{ id: "5F4B20CCBA5017D4", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3FE042093BEDCF50", item: "grindless:deployed_node_pack", type: "item" }]
			title: "Deployed Node Packs"
			x: 45.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1272CCD5EF9968D8"]
			description: ["With enough nodes running, the bulge collector records how much starlight the swarm gathers. The &6Bulge Light Census&r is the proof of a Kardashev III civilisation that the gate keeps."]
			icon: "grindless:bulge_light_census"
			id: "5651A00C576D3D7E"
			rewards: [{ id: "1678C430E0E724F7", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "5C20577FD762E577", item: "grindless:bulge_light_census", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bulge Light Census"
			x: 47.5d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5651A00C576D3D7E"]
			description: [
				"The Sagittarius A* chart is not on any shelf yet. When your power is ready, the warp gate waits for the Kugelblitz core, the light census, the stable exotic matter, a tetron array, census IV, the bulge chart and OpV-tier circuit tags."
				"It writes the chart and researches the &6MAX Machine Casing&r. Charge your SMES bank first."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:max_machine_casing"
			id: "3E3C190F1A77EB6D"
			rewards: [{ id: "36B8B96FA5CC20E9", type: "xp", xp: 400 }]
			shape: "diamond"
			size: 1.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "375203E342E9AE31", item: "gtceu:max_machine_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Gate to MAX"
			x: 50.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1A9EE7510BD6DBFC"]
			description: ["The wafers, chips and circuits of the era, from the first wafer to the mainframe, and the parts built from them."]
			icon: "minecraft:writable_book"
			id: "5DE7C491611D14C0"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "197780D52C5B0EAB", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Circuits"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -12.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5DE7C491611D14C0"]
			description: ["Natural silicon carries a few percent of silicon-29, whose nuclear spin disturbs a cold qubit. Purified silicon-28 on an insulating layer gives the &6Silicon-28 SOI Wafer&r that every cold chip is cut from. Silicon-28 from the centrifuge cascade, an oxide layer and the wafer bonder you already run. The cryo-CMOS wafer and the tetron chain. Keep a chest of wafers behind the bonder, since every later chip row draws from it."]
			icon: "grindless:si28_soi_wafer"
			id: "7D95B836E06310DB"
			rewards: [{ id: "3475373D8FC14F2C", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "3509AF9C7AA4FE39", item: "grindless:si28_soi_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Silicon-28 SOI Wafer"
			x: 7.5d
			y: -24.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7D95B836E06310DB"]
			description: ["Ordinary transistors stop working well near absolute zero, so the doping and the metal are tuned for the cold. The &6Cryo-CMOS Wafer&r is exposed, implanted and metallised in that order, and cut into dies. The lithography and implant lines of the age, and a silicon-28 wafer. The cryo-CMOS die, the logic of the cosmic mainframe. Stage by stage in one line, with the cut dies sent straight to the mainframe row."]
			icon: "grindless:cryo_cmos_metal_wafer"
			id: "3AD6042F25DCDFAE"
			rewards: [{ id: "5AE9D7EA62440A09", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3ACAF742691409BA", item: "grindless:cryo_cmos_metal_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "32946CDE111E80EB", item: "grindless:cryo_cmos_die", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Cryo-CMOS Wafer"
			x: 10.0d
			y: -25.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3AD6042F25DCDFAE"]
			description: ["A niobium interposer carries the signals through the die, a HEMT amplifier lifts them out of the noise, and an optical link takes them out of the cold without carrying heat in. The &6Niobium TSV Interposer&r, the &6HEMT Amplifier&r and the &6Cryo Optical Link&r are all ordinary assembler work once the dies exist."]
			icon: "grindless:cryo_optical_link"
			id: "328CDB4584A0E113"
			rewards: [{ id: "57487BE14A359C27", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3F4452F8C40138FF", item: "grindless:nb_tsv_interposer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "589FD06B4D89DAEC", item: "grindless:hemt_amplifier", type: "item" }
				{ id: "712C8D7A0D318AB9", item: "grindless:cryo_optical_link", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Cryogenic Links"
			x: 12.5d
			y: -26.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["328CDB4584A0E113"]
			description: ["A cryo-CMOS die, a niobium interposer, an amplifier and an optical link, all joined in one cold package. The &6Cosmic Mainframe&r is the OpV circuit. The cryo-CMOS die and the three parts of the row before it, on the assembly line. The OpV sensor and the controller of every machine past the hull. One of each part per mainframe, so keep a dedicated chest and never a big stock."]
			icon: "gtnn:cosmic_mainframe"
			id: "74C17E229844F7DF"
